    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1946-11-27">November 27th<lb/><hi rend="g"
                            >1945</hi></date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">
                        Paulus</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>Thanks for your note of <date when="1946-11-24">November 24</date>.<note
                        type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note> When I spoke to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1923" type="person">Hannah</rs> I forgot that we
                    had been informed through your secretary about the CARE packages. I apologize
                    for asking again.</p>
                <p>I am sad to report that we intend to go off to the country immediately after
                    Christmas. We will not be here to see you on <date from="1946-12-26"
                        to="1946-12-28">December 26–28</date>. I could put you up in the little
                    guest room of Pierson College but no meals will be served in the college at that
                    time. You would have no trouble, however, about picking up breakfast just around
                    the corner at the drug store. Let me know if you intend to stay in Pierson.</p>
                <p>I would be much interested to hear what you find out about guest professorships
                    in <rs type="place" ref="#tillich_place_id__122">Germany</rs>. I have informed
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__770" type="person">the Rector of the University
                        of</rs>
                    <rs type="place" ref="#tillich_place_id__143">Frankfurt</rs> that I shall not be
                    able to go there for some time to come. Apparently he got to assist in carrying
                    out a program of guest professorships. It is not only a question of
                    transportation but also of food and living quarters once one gets there. The
                    Germans cannot provide either.</p>
                <closer><salute>Hoping to see you soon, I remain,<lb/>As ever
                            yours,</salute><signed><hi rend="hand"><rs
                                ref="#tillich_person_id__2094" type="person"
                            >Arnold</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2094" type="person"
                            >Arnold Wolfers</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
